WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.500
In 1651, Thomas Hobbes described
life without government as solitary,

2
00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:09.240
poor, nasty, brutish, and short.

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:14.590
On 10 December 1948, the United
Nations adopted a declaration:

4
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:19.460
all human beings are born free
and equal in dignity and rights.

5
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:24.080
But Jeremy Bentham had called
natural rights nonsense upon stilts.

6
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.210
So if no law grants it,
do you still have a right?

7
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.450
In this mission, you'll meet
thinkers who answered differently,

8
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.890
from Hobbes to Bentham,
via Locke and Paine.

9
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:39.750
Then you'll test universal rights
against cultural and religious critiques.

10
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.360
Your mission: find out whether you
can have a right that no law grants.
